 ## Operating characteristics
 
-*   **Time Complexity:** The clustering phase involves a bottom-up traversal of the octree. For each non-leaf cell, vertices are clustered by combining QEFs and minimizing them. The complexity depends on the number of vertices and the depth of the octree. The polygon generation phase also traverses the octree, but can be optimized by truncating collapsed cells [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing the vertex tree, QEFs for each vertex, and octree structure. The vertex tree can grow significantly if many vertices are not collapsed [S1][S2, unofficial].
